# Requests for the "REST Client" extension of VS Code (humao.rest-client).
# Start the server with `npm run dev`, then click "Send Request" above any request.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Submit a request (expects 201 and a case number)
# @name submit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pqrs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "petition",
  "subject": "Copy of my property tax certificate",
  "description": "I need an official copy of my property tax certificate to complete a bank loan.",
  "requesterName": "Ana Gomez",
  "requesterEmail": "Ana.Gomez@Example.com"
}

### Validation errors (expects 400 with details)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pqrs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "other",
  "subject": "Hi",
  "description": "Too short",
  "requesterName": "",
  "requesterEmail": "not-an-email"
}

### Malformed JSON (expects 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pqrs
Content-Type: application/json

{ this is not json

### Anti-bot field filled in (expects 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pqrs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "petition",
  "subject": "Copy of my certificate",
  "description": "I need an official copy of my property tax certificate.",
  "requesterName": "Spam Bot",
  "requesterEmail": "bot@example.com",
  "website": "http://spam.example"
}

### Unknown route (expects 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/does-not-exist

### Look up the request you just submitted (expects 200; the email may use any case)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pqrs/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "caseNumber": "{{submit.response.body.caseNumber}}",
  "requesterEmail": "ANA.GOMEZ@example.com"
}

### Look up with the wrong email (expects 404, the same answer as an unknown case number)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pqrs/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "caseNumber": "{{submit.response.body.caseNumber}}",
  "requesterEmail": "someone.else@example.com"
}

### Look up with badly formed values (expects 400 with details)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pqrs/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "caseNumber": "12345",
  "requesterEmail": "not-an-email"
}

### Seeded demo request (run `npm run seed` first; expects 200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pqrs/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "caseNumber": "PQRS-2026-000001",
  "requesterEmail": "ana.gomez@example.com"
}


###
### Staff area (v0.2.0)
### Create an account first:  npm run admin -- create --email you@example.com --name "Your Name"
### Send the login, then copy "csrfToken" from its answer into @csrf below.
### The REST Client extension keeps the session cookie between requests.
###

@csrf = paste-the-csrfToken-here
@case = PQRS-2026-000001

### Staff login (expects 200, a cookie and a csrfToken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "you@example.com",
  "password": "your password"
}

### Who is logged in (expects 200, or 401 without a session)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/session

### Numbers for the dashboard
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/stats

### List with search, filters and pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/pqrs?q=tax&status=filed&type=petition&from=2026-01-01&to=2026-12-31&sort=createdAt&order=desc&page=1&pageSize=20

### One request with its history and the statuses it may move to
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/pqrs/{{case}}

### Change the status (expects 200, or 409 when the move is not allowed)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/pqrs/{{case}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "status": "in_progress",
  "expectedStatus": "filed"
}

### Without the CSRF token (expects 403)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/pqrs/{{case}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "in_progress" }

### Log out (expects 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/logout
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{}
